name issue_124_clean_link_v2
describe 2.5 Mbps link, 25 ms one-way, no impairments, every v2 switch on: the queue the flip (#61) leaves on a clean link (issue #124)
# `clean_link` with every v2 switch on, the configuration PR #116 makes the default. sm_compare traces
# this scenario packet by packet for both stacks (kDefaultTraced), so libwebrtc's send rate and
# bottleneck queue over time can be read from parity-data (tools/link_trace.py) and diffed with ours.
# Measured on main 2039b72 without `packetization v2` and `audio v2`, seeds 1-10 (ours / libwebrtc, parity-data of main):
#   cc.queue_p95_ms 84-185 (mean 119) / 45-107 (mean 76.7)
#   video.e2e_delay_p95_ms 123-214 (mean 157) / 105-148 (mean 125)
#   cc.utilization_pct 91.0-93.7 (mean 92.4) / 89.9-92.9 (mean 91.6)
# With the two switches on, and the test bench's video packet capacity at the 1458 B libwebrtc's trace shows
# (video wire size p50/p90/max 1375/1463/1486 B ours against 1374/1462/1486 B), seeds 1-10:
#   cc.queue_p95_ms 69-132 (mean 89) ; video.e2e_delay_p95_ms 107-168 (mean 126) ; cc.utilization_pct 91-93 (mean 92)
# Left (seeds 4 and 5): the target keeps rising about 25 kbps/s past the 2.5 Mbps link and overuse is signalled only
# when the queue is near 150 ms, so e2e p95 is 167 and 151 ms there.
# Seeds 11-40 (this run, main 74266b3): queue p95 mean 91.5, e2e p95 mean 129.7, utilization mean 91.9; e2e p95 >= 150 ms on 4 of 40 seeds
# (seeds 4, 5, 29 and 36), libwebrtc's 10 seeds top out at 148. The trendline, InterArrivalDelta, delay-detector, AIMD and feedback
# constants match the reference; the late seeds are slow ramps (about 25 kbps/s) that cross the link by 5-7% before the trendline
# slope reaches the 6 ms threshold floor, so the cycle between overuses is 22-25 s here against about 16 s in libwebrtc's seed-1 trace.
# Issue #124 root cause: the test bench sent each 20 ms audio packet at t = 0 mod 20 ms, the phase of the 30 fps video
# frames; libwebrtc's harness sends it at 10 mod 20 (10 ms ADM blocks). Replayed open loop through our GoogCC, libwebrtc's
# packets give libwebrtc's overuse times; ours, with the old phase, gave later ones. With the libwebrtc phase, seeds 1-10:
#   seeds 1-40: cc.queue_p95_ms mean 71.3 (max 106) / 71.3 ; video.e2e_delay_p95_ms mean 109.7 (max 140, none >= 150) / 121.5
#   (2 of 40 >= 150) ; cc.utilization_pct mean 91.2 / 91.6.
# The lines below lock the level reached on seeds 1-40.
# Target (issue #124): cc.queue_p95_ms, video.e2e_delay_p95_ms and cc.utilization_pct within the parity band
# of libwebrtc, and `video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 150` on every seed (the line `clean_link` carries).
# sm_compare runs 40 seeds of both stacks here (the Owner's 13:16 UTC brief on #124), to judge the "every seed" line against libwebrtc's own distribution.
compare_seeds 40
cc v2
pacer v2
rtx v2
keyframe v2
allocator v2
packetization v2
audio v2
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect video.freeze_count == 0
expect cc.unsettled == 0
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 86
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 150
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 120
